DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The bbssdd..rree--ccoonnffiigg file contains kernel modification commands in config(8)
     format.  If present, it is used during system startup to configure the
     kernel that will be running at the next boot.  It can be used to enable
     or disable specific devices in the kernel.

